`Number.isInteger(maxPresetColors)` rejects non-integer floats, silently falling back to `27`. A user who passes `maxPresetColors: 5.7` (e.g., the result of a calculation) will see 27 presets instead of the expected ~5. Use `Math.floor(maxPresetColors)` and then validate that the floored result is `> 0`, rather than outright rejecting the value:

```ts
const floored = Math.floor(maxPresetColors);
const limit = floored > 0 ? floored : 27;
return combined.slice(-limit);
```

This makes the behavior predictable and avoids silent large-number surprises.
